Falsifies `address_space_map::verification::every_address_below_the_ceiling_lies_in_exactly_one_band`.

The defect: `SERVICE_WINDOWS` starts one page below the heap's end, so the two bands share a page.
The `const` tiling assert in `lib.rs` would stop the build first, so the patch deletes it as well:
what this shows is that the harness catches an overlap on its own.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(bands_containing(va), 1)`, at `va = 0x4FFF_F000..0x5000_0000`.

diff --git a/crates/address_space_map/src/lib.rs b/crates/address_space_map/src/lib.rs
index 0eba0def7..4fae2decf 100644
--- a/crates/address_space_map/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/address_space_map/src/lib.rs
@@ -88,7 +88,7 @@ pub const HEAP: Band = Band {
 /// the block channel (`0x5000_0000`, 8 MiB, used by the filesystem server, the installer, the disk
 /// partitioner and `mkfs`), the C seam's grant pages, the screen aperture.
 pub const SERVICE_WINDOWS: Band = Band {
-    start: HEAP.end,
+    start: HEAP.end - PAGE,
     end: 0x6000_0000,
 };
 
@@ -282,10 +282,6 @@ const _: () = {
     let mut i = 0;
     while i < BANDS.len() {
         let band = BANDS[i].1;
-        assert!(
